      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "If $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{8},$ then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+12\\pi )=$",
      "worked_solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+2\\cdot 6\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=-\\frac{5}{8},$ then $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+12\\pi )=-\\frac{5}{8}.$",
